# Proposed NIDM vocabulary entry for the new image-usage type `nidm:FieldMap`.
#
# WHERE THIS GOES: the NIDM-Experiment / NIDM-Terms vocabulary (the external
# repo that formally defines the other image-usage types nidm:Anatomical,
# nidm:Functional, nidm:DiffusionWeighted). It is NOT defined inside PyNIDM --
# PyNIDM only emits the URI. This file is a hand-off artifact so the term can
# be added to the vocabulary and documented rather than being an undefined URI.
#
# ACTION: copy the existing `nidm:DiffusionWeighted` definition from the
# vocabulary source and mirror it for `nidm:FieldMap`, adjusting label/comment.
# The block below is a reasonable proposal; align its rdf:type / parent
# (owl:Class vs owl:NamedIndividual, rdfs:subClassOf ...) with however the
# sibling usage types are actually modeled in the source vocabulary.

@prefix nidm: <http://purl.org/nidash/nidm#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

nidm:FieldMap
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Field Map"@en ;
    rdfs:comment
        "An MRI acquisition intended to map B0 magnetic-field inhomogeneity (a field map), used for susceptibility-distortion correction of EPI-based scans. Corresponds to the BIDS field-map suffixes: fieldmap, magnitude, magnitude1, magnitude2, phasediff, phase1, phase2, and epi. Used as an nidm:hadImageUsageType value alongside nidm:Anatomical, nidm:Functional, and nidm:DiffusionWeighted."@en ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy nidm: .

# If the sibling usage types are modeled as instances of a shared class
# (e.g. nidm:ImageUsageType) rather than owl:Class, use instead:
#
# nidm:FieldMap
#     a nidm:ImageUsageType ;
#     rdfs:label "Field Map"@en ;
#     rdfs:comment "..."@en .
